    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "editorial-83",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s82",
          "text": "Is cleaning still worth considering on an older sofa?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "editorial-85",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s84",
          "text": "The useful question is what is making the sofa look tired. Everyday soil and body oils can respond to cleaning. A worn seam, flattened cushion or faded patch is a different concern and should be pointed out before you book.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "editorial-90",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_type": "link",
          "_key": "l87",
          "href": "/blog/what-to-expect-when-softnest-cleans-your-sofa/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s86",
          "text": "You can ask us to assess the material and discuss what improvement is realistic. If you're weighing cleaning against repair or replacement, tell us what you hope to change. A clear expectation is more useful than a promise that an older sofa will look new. Our ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s88",
          "text": "appointment guide",
          "marks": [
            "l87"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s89",
          "text": " explains the inspection and cleaning process.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    }
